usage: aethertwin-serve [-h] [--mode {sim,replay,live}] [--config CONFIG]
                        [--input INPUT] [--twin TWIN]
                        [--checkpoint CHECKPOINT] [--record RECORD]
                        [--commissioning-static-recording COMMISSIONING_STATIC_RECORDING]
                        [--calibration-correspondences CALIBRATION_CORRESPONDENCES]
                        [--output OUTPUT] [--host HOST] [--port PORT]
                        [--device {cpu,cuda,auto}] [--threads THREADS]
                        [--max-frames MAX_FRAMES] [--seed SEED]
                        [--duration DURATION] [--ssl-certfile SSL_CERTFILE]
                        [--ssl-keyfile SSL_KEYFILE]
                        [--allowed-origin ALLOWED_ORIGIN] [--access-log]
                        [--open-browser]

Run the AetherTwin local/private browser command center.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --mode {sim,replay,live}
  --config CONFIG
  --input INPUT
  --twin TWIN
  --checkpoint CHECKPOINT
  --record RECORD       Record raw source segments under a new session
                        directory
  --commissioning-static-recording COMMISSIONING_STATIC_RECORDING
                        Declare an explicitly static recording for
                        commissioning jobs
  --calibration-correspondences CALIBRATION_CORRESPONDENCES
                        Register measured correspondence NPZ for candidate
                        export
  --output OUTPUT
  --host HOST
  --port PORT
  --device {cpu,cuda,auto}
  --threads THREADS
  --max-frames MAX_FRAMES
  --seed SEED
  --duration DURATION   Bound processing by wall-clock seconds; keep the
                        viewer available
  --ssl-certfile SSL_CERTFILE
  --ssl-keyfile SSL_KEYFILE
  --allowed-origin ALLOWED_ORIGIN
                        Explicit trusted HTTPS gateway origin; may repeat
  --access-log          Log each HTTP request (off by default)
  --open-browser        Open the local command center after the server is
                        ready
